<title>AUSTRIA: OPEC HQ DENIES VENEZUELA ADMITTED OVERPRODUCING.</title>
<headline>OPEC HQ DENIES VENEZUELA ADMITTED OVERPRODUCING.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The OPEC Secretariat on Thursday &quot;categorically denied&quot; reports claiming Venezuela had admitted pumping 800,000 barrels per day above its quota at the group's summer conference here.  </p>
<p>The OPEC news agency said that the reports claim the admission was made during a three-hour closed session on Wednesday which was attended only by delegation heads and OPEC's Secretary General.</p>
<p>&quot;So any information quoting other sources lacked any credibility,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>On Wednesday, a Gulf source said Venezuela had made the admission while adding that it would &quot;try to&quot; commit to its 2.359 million barrels per day (bpd) allocation.</p>
<p>Earlier today, OPEC ended its conference. It formally agreed to freeze its 25.033 million bpd ceiling for the rest of the year, with members &quot;undertaking to restrain output to their agreed level of allocation&quot;.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom +431 713 2002</p>
